## 1. Global infrastructure (do these first — later fixes depend on them)

### 1.1 Build the missing 404 page
There is currently no `app/not-found.tsx`. Next.js falls back to its default blank error page for every broken link in the app — including several you're about to fix links *toward* pages that don't exist until Phase 5.

Create `app/not-found.tsx`:
- Full-bleed centered layout, same visual language as `EmptyState` but full-page (glass card is optional; plain centered content is fine, look at how `login/page.tsx` centers its card for the vertical-centering pattern).
- Icon: a `Compass` or `SearchX` from `lucide-react`.
- Heading: "This page doesn't exist." Body: one sentence, honest tone matching the rest of the copy voice (e.g. "The link might be old, or the page hasn't been built yet.").
- Include the global search trigger inline: a button that calls `usePalette((s) => s.setOpen)(true)` from `components/app/command-palette.tsx` labeled "Search instead", styled like the topbar's search pill.
- Two `PillLink`s below: if `useSession((s) => s.authed)` is true, link to `/app` labeled "Back to dashboard"; otherwise link to `/` labeled "Back home".
- This must be a `'use client'` component since it reads from the session store.

### 1.2 Build a real `ConfirmDialog` component
Two places currently use the browser's native `confirm()` (`app/app/bots/page.tsx`'s delete handler, `components/bot/settings-tab.tsx`'s delete handler). Native `confirm()` is unstyled, blocks the JS thread, and looks like a bug next to a glass UI.

Create `components/ui/confirm-dialog.tsx`:
```
interface ConfirmDialogProps {
  open: boolean
  onOpenChange: (open: boolean) => void
  title: string
  description: string
  confirmLabel?: string       // default "Confirm"
  cancelLabel?: string        // default "Cancel"
  destructive?: boolean       // default true — red confirm button
  onConfirm: () => void
}
```
Build it on top of the existing `Dialog`/`DialogContent`/`DialogHeader`/`DialogTitle`/`DialogDescription`/`DialogFooter`/`Button` primitives — same composition pattern as `UnlockDialog` and the "Save as block" dialog already in `builder/[botId]/page.tsx`. The confirm button uses `variant="destructive"` when `destructive` is true (the `Button` component already supports this variant — check `components/ui/button.tsx`).

Then replace both native `confirm()` call sites:
- `app/app/bots/page.tsx` → `handleDelete`: hold `{ id, name } | null` in state, render one `ConfirmDialog` at the bottom of the page, title `Delete "${name}"?`, description `"This permanently removes the bot, its saved versions, and its backtest history. This can't be undone."`
- `components/bot/settings-tab.tsx` → `handleDelete`: same pattern, plus route back to `/app/bots` only after confirm (this already happens, just move it inside the `onConfirm` callback).

### 1.3 Real auth gating
Right now `useSession`'s `authed` defaults to `true` and nothing ever checks it to gate a route. The Dev Panel (`components/dev/dev-panel.tsx`) has a working "Signed in: Yes/No" toggle that currently does nothing observable — flipping it to "No" doesn't kick you out of `/app`. "Sign out" in `AccountMenu` (`components/app/app-topbar.tsx`) sets `authed: false` and pushes to `/`, but if the user then types `/app` in the address bar or hits back, they're back in with nothing stopping them.

Fix in `app/app/layout.tsx`: convert it to (or wrap it in) a client component that checks `useSession`:
```
const authed = useSession((s) => s.authed)
const hydrated = useSession((s) => s.hydrated)
const router = useRouter()

useEffect(() => {
  if (hydrated && !authed) router.replace('/login')
}, [hydrated, authed, router])

if (!hydrated) return <FullPageSkeleton />   // avoid a flash of the workspace before hydration resolves
if (!authed) return null                      // redirect is in flight
```
Since `app/app/layout.tsx` is currently a server component exporting `metadata`, split it: keep a thin server `layout.tsx` for the `metadata` export, move the actual JSX + guard into a new client component `components/app/app-shell.tsx` that the layout renders. This mirrors how `bots/[botId]/page.tsx` already separates a `Suspense`-wrapped inner component from its default export — same pattern, applied one level up.

While you're in here, also gate on onboarding: if `authed && !onboardingComplete`, redirect to `/onboarding` instead of rendering the workspace (the `/onboarding` route itself is built in Phase 5 — this redirect will 404 gracefully via your new `not-found.tsx` until then, which is fine and expected).

### 1.4 Wire login/signup into the onboarding gate
`app/login/page.tsx` and `app/signup/page.tsx` both currently do `setAuthed(true); router.push('/app')`. Change the signup flow specifically (login stays as-is, since a returning user has presumably already onboarded):
```
setAuthed(true)
router.push(onboardingComplete ? '/app' : '/onboarding')
```
`onboardingComplete` defaults to `true` in `INITIAL` in `lib/store.ts` today — leave the default as `true` for now (so nothing breaks before Phase 5 builds `/onboarding`), but make sure the Dev Panel's existing "Onboarded: No" toggle, once flipped, actually routes a fresh sign-in through `/onboarding`. This is one line of behavior to get right now so Phase 5 doesn't have to touch auth logic again.

