## 2. Marketing/landing page dead links

### 2.1 The two biggest dead links on the entire site
`components/landing/hero.tsx` and `components/landing/closing-cta.tsx` link their primary CTAs to `/builder` and `/marketplace` — **neither route exists**. There is no `app/builder/page.tsx` at the root (only `app/app/builder/page.tsx`), and no `app/marketplace/page.tsx` at the root (only `app/app/marketplace/page.tsx`). Every visitor who clicks "Open the builder" or "Browse strategies" on the homepage currently hits a blank error page. This is the single highest-impact fix in this entire phase — it's the primary conversion path on the marketing site.

Fix, in both files:
- `"/builder"` → route smartly based on auth: if `authed`, `/app/builder`; if not, `/signup`. Since both are server-rendered-looking marketing sections that are actually `'use client'` already (check — `hero.tsx` uses `motion` so it's already client), read `useSession((s) => s.authed)` and compute the href, or simplest: keep it a plain link to `/app/builder` — the new auth guard from §1.3 will now correctly bounce an unauthed visitor to `/login` instead of silently 404ing, which is an acceptable and common pattern (click "open builder" while logged out → land on login, not stuck). Either approach is fine; the smart-route version is slightly better UX. Pick the smart-route version since you're already touching `lib/store.ts`.
- `"/marketplace"` → `/app/marketplace` for now (the dedicated public, logged-out-friendly marketplace page from the sitemap is built in Phase 5 at `/marketplace`; once that lands, point these back to the new public route instead — leave a `// TODO(phase5): point at public /marketplace once built` comment so it's not forgotten).

### 2.2 The sitewide nav "Marketplace" link
`components/marketing/site-nav.tsx`'s `LINKS` array also points "Marketplace" at `/marketplace`, and it renders on **every marketing page** (it's fixed/sticky). Apply the same fix as §2.1.

### 2.3 The marketplace teaser section
`components/landing/marketplace-teaser.tsx` has two more instances: "Browse all presets" → `/marketplace`, and each preset card → `/marketplace/${p.id}`. Same fix as above for the list link. For the per-card links, since `/marketplace/:id` (public detail) is a Phase 5 page too, leave these as `/marketplace/${p.id}` — they'll 404 gracefully until Phase 5, same TODO comment.

### 2.4 Footer inconsistency
`components/marketing/site-footer.tsx`'s `COLUMNS` has both a "Blog" link and a "Changelog" link pointing at the exact same `/blog` href — two different labels promising two different things and landing on the same (currently nonexistent) page. Once Phase 5 builds `/blog`, that's the correct target for "Blog". For "Changelog", point it at `/blog?category=Product` instead (there's no dedicated changelog data model, and `BlogPost.category` already includes a `'Product'` category that covers product-update-style posts) — or simplest, since query-param filtering isn't in scope for the blog list page's spec in Phase 5, just point "Changelog" at `/docs` for now with a one-line comment noting it's a placeholder until a real changelog exists. Don't build a changelog system — that's out of scope for all four phases.

