## 3. Pricing is shown three different ways with three different numbers

This is a real, visible bug: a visitor scrolling the homepage sees Starter at **₹799**/mo and Pro at **₹1,999**/mo (`components/landing/pricing-teaser.tsx`, which correctly reads from `PLANS` in `mock/data.ts`). The same visitor clicking through to `/pricing` sees Starter at **₹2,999**/mo and Pro at **₹9,999**/mo (`app/pricing/page.tsx`, fully hardcoded, ignores `PLANS` entirely). A logged-in user on `/app/billing` sees the same wrong ₹2,999/₹9,999 numbers (`app/app/billing/page.tsx`, also fully hardcoded, also ignores `PLANS`). Three surfaces, two different prices, zero of them agree with each other.

**`PLANS` in `mock/data.ts` is the single source of truth from now on.** Fix both:

### 3.1 `app/pricing/page.tsx`
Rewrite to map over `PLANS` (excluding `payg` for the main three-card row, matching what `pricing-teaser.tsx` already does) instead of three hand-written `<div>`s. Each card's feature list comes from `plan.features` (already an array of strings — no hardcoded `<span>` list needed). Add:
- A monthly/annual `Segmented` toggle (from `components/ui/tabs.tsx`) above the cards — `Plan` already has both `monthly` and `annual` fields, currently only `monthly` is shown anywhere. Toggling switches which number renders, with the annual number divided by 12 for the "/mo" display and a small "billed annually" note, standard SaaS pattern.
- Below the three cards, render the full `PLAN_COMPARISON` grouped table (`group` + `rows`, each row has `free`/`starter`/`pro`/`payg` — string or boolean; `true` renders as a `Check` icon, `false` renders as a muted `—`, a string renders as-is). This data exists and currently has zero consumers anywhere in the app — it was written for exactly this table.
- A fourth "Pay-as-you-go" card or a smaller inline callout beneath the three main cards, using `PLANS.find(p => p.id === 'payg')` — currently entirely unused.
- Reuse `Faq` section content by rendering `FAQS` again here (same component pattern as the landing page's `Faq`, or extract the FAQ accordion markup from `components/landing/faq.tsx` into a shared component `components/marketing/faq-accordion.tsx` that both `/` and `/pricing` use — do this extraction, since you now have two consumers).

### 3.2 `app/app/billing/page.tsx`
Rewrite the "Subscription Plans Matrix" section to map over `PLANS` the same way, so the logged-in billing page finally agrees with the marketing pricing page. Keep the existing `handlePlanChange` logic (it already calls `setPlan` and toasts correctly) — just drive the card content from data instead of three copy-pasted blocks.

Also fix the credit purchase buttons in the same file: they're hardcoded to "+100 Credits (₹499)" and "+500 Credits (₹1,999)" with the second one mislabeled (`CREDIT_BUNDLES` in `mock/data.ts` says 500 credits costs ₹499 and 1000 credits costs ₹999 — the current UI's price for 500 credits, ₹1,999, matches neither the 500-credit nor the 1000-credit bundle). Map over `CREDIT_BUNDLES` instead of hand-writing two buttons; this also picks up the `popular` flag on the 500-credit bundle for free.

